# Help > Report a Bug (the reference's 0.8.9): a sheet that files a Knots
# issue as the person at the keyboard. It shows what will be sent -- the text,
# which board, whether the window capture rides along, the context lines --
# and the capture, uploaded first, travels as a link in the description. The
# fake runner answers; a scripted run never runs the real CLI.
#
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":["t2"],"active_tab":"t2","theme":"dark"}

require_thread t2
open_bug_report
wait_frames 10
expect_text "Report a bug"
expect_text "Files to gabeochoa/manager."
expect_text "Filed from: menu"
# Nothing typed: Send does nothing.
click_ui bug_report_send
wait_frames 6
assert_ui bug_report_panel hidden=false

click_ui bug_report_text
type "The sidebar flickers"
wait_frames 6
click_ui bug_report_board_backend
wait_frames 6
expect_text "Files to agentcloud/client."
click_ui bug_report_send
wait_frames 40
expect_no_ui bug_report_panel
expect_toast_holds "Filed kt-mock1"
expect_mock_knot_arg Screenshot: [hanabi-window.png](https://www.internalfb.com/F1000001)
expect_mock_knot_arg agentcloud/client
expect_mock_knot_arg The sidebar flickers
